{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Elohim</b> — as in the usage: \"Your enemies blaspheme Your name forever,\" who is the King of Israel." "<b>Working salvation</b> — known on our behalf, in the midst of the earth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {0 "The phrase כדרך (\"as in the usage\") likely refers back to the preceding verse (74:10) about enemies blaspheming God's name; I read ינאץ as a variant of ינאץ/יחרף (\"blaspheme/revile\")."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:27.783544699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}